---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const R = 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments/tree/main/';
const hrefOf = (p: string) => (p.startsWith('http') || p.startsWith('/')) ? p : R + p;
const labelOf = (p: string) => p.replace(/^https:\/\/github\.com\//, '');
const groups = [
  { id: 'agency', aliases: [], title: 'Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents', paper: '/papers/agency/', rows: [
    ['§8.11 preregistered acceptor run', 'agency-run/', 'Preregistrations v1, v2 and second machine; agents, meters, tasks, analysis; episodes and receipts'],
    ['§8.11 results, run 1', 'agency-run/results/', 'Episode rows and receipts'],
    ['§8.11.1 and §8.11.2 results', 'agency-run/results2/', 'Second run; the second machine is in results_jetson/ and results_jetson_cyc/'],
  ]},
  { id: 'rce', aliases: [], title: 'The Reality Code Engine', paper: '/papers/rce/', rows: [
    ['Reference checker, emitters, and 5,537 Lean 4 theorems (T1 to T63)', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce/tree/1762fb4b', 'Commit 1762fb4b: 2,221/2,236 passing conformance checks (0 fail), 837 Rust checker unit tests, browser Wasm checker'],
    ['Apple M5 Max reported_j checker and 62-Form suite receipts', 'rce/bench/reported-j/', '49.04 mJ / 7.32 ms per Form check; 15.44 J / 2.32 s per full 62-Form check + run + 5-target emit suite (measured_j unset)'],
    ['§6 repair ladder protocol (L0 and L1)', 'rce/bench/ladder/', 'LADDER.md, PREREG.json with splits, report.py'],
    ['§5.5 model proposer on the demonstration specification', 'rce/bench/results/', 'llm-proposer-form-demo.form.json: 18 proposals, 13 distinct, 15 not admitted, one rewrite admitted under three names'],
    ['Cross-backend conformance of RCE graph code (first written under the name flowG; not cited by the RCE paper)', 'flowg-conformance/', 'Suite, fixtures by tier, recorded 18 of 18 report, CI job'],
    ['§3.8 dimension runs dim-r2 to dim-r5', 'rce/bench/dimension/', 'PREREG.json with amendments and hash sidecar, RESULTS.md, per-program rows in results/'],
    ['§3.5, §3.7 and §12.4 surveys of 22, 23 and 24 October 2026', 'rce/surveys/', 'The three design reports, the database survey, the versioning survey (continuous improvement without versions), the new-entrant languages survey (111 languages of 2024 to 2026) and their reading notes'],
  ]},
  { id: 'rce-jepa', aliases: [], title: 'RCE-JEPA', paper: '/papers/rce-jepa/', rows: [
    ['W1 Form corpus v1 and v2, H1 (Form space against source space), the intent mutation score and the cost of a check', 'rce/bench/form-space/', 'PREREG.json with amendments and hash sidecar, CARD.md (dataset card), RESULTS.md, results/forms.jsonl, results/negatives.jsonl, summary.json; generator scripts/corpus.py in openIE-dev/rce'],
    ['H2 checker-to-proposer reported_j ratio on Apple M5 Max', 'rce/bench/reported-j/', '0.04904 J per Form check vs 84.25 J local Qwen 3.6 proposal (C_check / E_model = 0.000582 <= 0.05); measured_j unset'],
    ['H7 adversarial Forms, fuzzed arm: 560 accepted mutants against five invariants', 'rce/bench/adversarial/', 'PREREG.json with hash sidecar, run.py, RESULTS.md, results/summary.json and violations.jsonl (empty)'],
    ['H8 determinism: 10,500 streams on six targets', 'rce/bench/determinism/', 'PREREG.json with hash sidecar, RESULTS.md with the workflow run, per-target jobs and limits; generator scripts/xarch-streams.py and the parity workflow in openIE-dev/rce'],
    ['H15 (k = 1) residual 40-task multi-vendor benchmark & Shape D (DNULLMM1) Gear-0 replay', 'rce/bench/h15-gear0/', 'PREREG.json (b64c4c67...), residual_40_tasks.jsonl, multi-vendor proposer episodes (Opus 5.5 34/40, Sonnet 5.5 32/40, Grok 4.20 31/40, GPT-OSS-120B 29/40, Qwen 3.6 27/40, DeepSeek V4.1 17/40), and 0-call Gear-0 store (34/40 replay, 7/9 nameless alpha-rename hits, 4.17x Zipf call reduction)'],
    ['FormJEPA-v1 latent Form proposer, 3-Gear Cascade, and rce repair rung-f criterion audit', 'rce/bench/form-jepa-v1/', 'PREREG_form_jepa_v1.json (22682e6e...), PREREG_rung_f.json (04aff4b2...), 8.42M-param PyTorch JEPA training & evaluation scripts on 1,387 disjoint Forms (177/200 unseen synthetic defects, 138/151 with ladder, 27/40 residual H15 at 474.8 mJ RAPL core reported_j, 8.70x Zipf 3-Gear call reduction), and 151-task rung-f observation audit (holds: false at 3/119 = 2.5% > 2.0%, 3/3 mutation-gate pass, 0 contradictions)'],
  ]},
  { id: 'rce-vc', aliases: [], title: 'RCE-VC', paper: '/papers/rce-vc/', rows: [
    ['Milestones M0 to M2 reference implementation', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-vc/tree/aba99fce', 'Commit aba99fce: 49 offline tests across rcevc-core, rcevc-keys, and rcevc-proj-git'],
    ['100,000-unit admission timing and L3 reported_j receipts', 'rce/bench/reported-j/', '69.7 to 73.6 microseconds and 317 to 365 microjoules per admission on Apple M5 Max (measured_j unset)'],
  ]},
  { id: 'rce-compile', aliases: ['three-body'], title: 'RCE Compile and The Three-Body Problem in Computing', paper: '/papers/rce-compile/', rows: [
    ['Byte comparisons, erasure counts, name-free hash checks, and cited verified-systems protocols', '/papers/rce-compile/', 'Section 8 of RCE Compile records compiler byte-determinism, description-length counts, and name-free hash tests; Three-Body cites public CompCert, seL4, and AWS TLA+ artefacts.'],
  ]},
  { id: 'gates', aliases: [], title: 'Metered Commit Gates', paper: '/papers/gates/', rows: [
    ['Part I and II plus browser Wasm + WebGPU commit-gate simulator', '/living/fpga-sim/', 'The gate and cascade use the WCA reference implementation and golden seed-1 vectors; KV260 INA260 board logs are cited in Appendix A.'],
  ]},
  { id: 'deterministic-null', aliases: [], title: 'Deterministic Null: A Pre-Registered Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates', paper: '/papers/deterministic-null/', rows: [
    ['Gate G2 five-language conformance & 1M DNULLMM1 mmap probes', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null', 'Rust, C++20, Go, Julia, and Python implementations reproducing frozen store digest 0da4df8d9ccbce1e...4485781 and 10k-probe checksum 15027705736.'],
    ['Gate G1 Track-A (reg-exp-001, drand 6663734), Track-B (reg-exp-002, drand 6664089), and exp-003 closures', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null/tree/main/receipts', 'Manifest digests cffb564cd9ad... (.ots 172 B) and 5fe640f00298... (.ots 207 B), 4,030 held-out instances, multi-vendor Track-B (OpenAI gpt-oss-120b, xAI Grok 4.20), 49/50 extended-thinking and 50/50 O(m) clause-feedback Unique 3-SAT DRAT resolution, and 5/6 real upstream SWE-bench Verified pytest patches. Local Apple M5 Max counters are reported_j; measured_j is unset.'],
  ]},
  { id: 'satb-harness', aliases: [], title: 'Satiation Benchmark: Reference Harness, Adapters, and Telemetry Attribution', paper: '/papers/satb-harness/', rows: [
    ['Lane B Rust harness & satb-proxy source', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null', 'Reference sequential harness (ContextRule_v0 80% elision + Truncate_v0 8+8 KiB) and loopback adapter bridge'],
    ['C1-C12 conformance, Falsifiers 3/5/6/8, and live multi-vendor C12 determinism receipts', 'satb-harness/', 'bench_satb_falsifiers.py and satb_empirical_receipts.json: 12/12 C1-C12 checks, 0-100 Hz observer-effect curve, Kepler proportional vs boundary comparison, 188-window Falsifier 6 audit, and Claude Code 2.1.330 completion parity'],
    ['Four-archetype hardware attribution & NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor INA238/INA3221 measured_j receipts', 'satb-harness/multi-host/', 'multi_host_satb_receipts.json and run_multi_host_satb.py across Apple M5 Max (IOReport/rusage reported_j), Jetson AGX Thor (TI INA238 VIN L1 and 3-channel INA3221 L2 shunt measured_j on shared host), Framework AMD Ryzen AI Max+ 395 (0440 root:energy RAPL reported_j + Radeon 8060S PPT), and Intel Core i9-13900H (psys L1 + package-0 L2 RAPL reported_j)'],
  ]},
  { id: 'time-as-an-index', aliases: [], title: 'Time as an Index: What It Would Take to Look Up Tomorrow', paper: '/papers/time-as-an-index/', rows: [
    ['Lean 4.36.0 formal verification (31 theorems, zero sorry)', 'time-as-an-index/lean/', 'Horizon.lean (17 theorems across C1-C4, H-coarse, M1, M3-M6) and Paradox.lean (14 theorems across self-referential oracles, pigeonhole incompressibility, recurrence, and measure)'],
    ['Models M1 to M8 + F5 SHA-256 spectral suite & 195-entry CSV catalogs', 'time-as-an-index/', 'run_models_m1_m8.py, models_m1_m8_results.json (seed 20261122), temporal-anomaly-catalog.csv (TA001-TA081), anomaly-atlas.csv (AA01-AA40), and paradox-ledger.csv (P01-P74)'],
  ]},
  { id: 'lut-adapt', aliases: [], title: 'Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade', paper: '/papers/lut-adapt/', rows: [
    ['Claims LA-1 to LA-11, Yosys/Verilator xck26 RTL, Expert-AirMoL 35B NVMe, Sub1Bit-LUT6, and 48-task 87.50% bakeoff', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai/tree/af152ba', 'Public reference and CSV/JSON/RTL/.mol artifacts at commit af152ba (artifacts/). Reports 87.50% (42/48) verified coding pass, 0.00% broken commits, 2.89 ms / 0.0424 J reported_j Wave-3 replay, and labeled est_j estimates (measured_j unset).'],
    ['Claims LA-12 to LA-14: Metal INT4 MoE & GatedDeltaNet shaders, Apple M5 Max reported_j, 16-task SWE-Mini pytest suite, and OpenAI/MCP mol-agent', 'https://github.com/openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai/tree/af152ba/artifacts', 'metal_moe_air_mol_speedup.csv (970.0 MB = 1.47% FP16 RAM, 6.773 J/tok reported_j on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), repo_patch_swebench_mini.csv (87.50% = 14/16 git-repo pytest pass, 0.00% broken patches, 594 ms / 1.10 J .mol/ replay), and mol-agent OpenAI /v1 + MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 server (26/26 pytest pass; measured_j unset)'],
    ['Section 4.15 xck26-sfvc784-2LV-c full-subsystem primitive & topological-depth audit + Vivado 2026.1 OOC Tcl', 'lut-adapt-vivado-audit/', 'Yosys xcup utilization and logic-level reports for clai_benes_paged_hotswap_core (41,185 CLB LUTs, 81 RAMB36E2s, 81 levels) and clai_kv260_axi_top (67,366 CLB LUTs, 126 IOBs, 73 levels), read-only hw_server JTAG scan, and run_vivado_xck26.tcl'],
  ]},
  { id: 'game-engines', aliases: [], title: 'Writing a Game Once and Running It Everywhere: Where Exact Replay Ends and Tolerance Begins', paper: '/papers/game-engines/', rows: [
    ['GE-H1 25-cell multi-ISA Q32.32 determinism, cross-ISA GE-H2 float drift, and 4-GPU headless wgpu GE-H3 tolerance', 'game-engines-determinism/', 'PREREG_wave3_multi_isa_wgpu.json (1721e5bd...), 5-machine / 3-ISA SHA-256 checkpoint receipts (0/20,500 mismatches), cross-OS libm & FMA divergence logs, and ge_h3_wgpu_bench across Apple Metal, AMD RADV Vulkan, NVIDIA RTX 4050 Vulkan, and Intel ANV Vulkan (24/24 frame pairs passing PSNR 64.16-72.06 dB, SSIM >= 0.999833)'],
    ['Playable 60 Hz Q32.32 Chrono-Budget Arena & WebXR observatory', '/living/game-engines/', 'Browser BigInt orbital simulation with per-tick SHA-256 verification, Hellman lookahead + Landauer branch-erasure joule budgeting, and WebXR gamepad support'],
  ]},
  { id: 'ai-reads-human', aliases: [], title: '"AI" Reads Human: Human Language Encoding at Machine Speed and the Energy Cost', paper: '/papers/ai-reads-human/', rows: [
    ['Section 5c 34-workload dual-channel reported_j harness and 170-window receipts', 'ai-reads-human-energy/', 'bench_energy_reported_j.py, energy_reported_j.tsv, raw_replicates.jsonl, and summary.json (L3 ri_energy_nj and L2 IOReport; measured_j unset)'],
    ['20,000-record parse-time corpus, token counts, and format-hazard test suites', '/living/ai-reads-human/', 'Downloadable TSV tables, reproduction scripts, READ_LEDGER.md, and cited specification edge-case tests'],
  ]},
  { id: 'mei', aliases: ['jouleos'], title: 'Metabolic Intelligence and The Search for JouleOS: JCP Receipt Spine & MEI-JCP-Tag-v1 Hardware Reference', paper: '/products/mei/', rows: [
    ['jcp-satb-cad-spine (310 tests), cad-joules bridge patch, and MEI-JCP-Tag-v1 PCB/3D/cold-chain package', 'jcp-cad-mei-tag/', '78,400-pair provenance meet-semilattice, canonical det-CBOR + Ed25519 JCR-1 receipts, DRC-certified (0 violations) 32 x 24 mm 2-layer STM32WBA52 + TI INA238 + FRAM PCB Gerbers/KiCad/BOM/CPL, 3D NURBS STEP/STL enclosure, and 10,000-wakeup CR2032 electro-thermal verification (board_metered is false; measured_j is unset)'],
    ['Interactive Cold-Chain JCP Budget & MEI-JCP-Tag-v1 Hardware Explorer', '/living/mei/', 'Interactive PCB/enclosure/JCR-1 explorer and temperature-dependent CR2032 voltage-sag simulator'],
  ]},
  { id: 'latency', aliases: [], title: 'The Gap Between Possible and Deployed', paper: '/papers/latency/', rows: [
    ['Dated release/lag tables and interactive cadence/cost simulator', '/living/latency/', 'Model release and benchmark frontier tables (also archived under timeline/ in openIE-dev/deterministic-null) plus interactive cadence and per-task cost breakdown'],
  ]},
  { id: 'economics', aliases: ['satiation', 'spellcheck', 'ai-coding-market', 'interface-economics'], title: 'Economics and history essays: Task Satiation, Spell Check, AI-Coding Market, Interface Economics', paper: '/papers/ai-coding-market/', rows: [
    ['Interactive companion figures and cited public sources', '/living/', 'Interactive figures at /living/satiation/ and /living/spellcheck/; projections and historical prices cite public sources in each paper\'s reference list.'],
  ]},
];
---
<Layout title="Data and code | OpenIE Research" description="Where each paper's results live in the public experiments and reference repositories.">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-white">Data and code</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The reproducible material for these studies lives in <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments">github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments</a> and companion repositories under <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev">github.com/openIE-dev</a> (<a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce">rce</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-vc">rce-vc</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null">deterministic-null</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai">lut-adapt-ai</a>): preregistrations with SHA-256 digests, scripts, Lean 4 proof packages, CAD/ECAD hardware files, results, receipts, a repository-wide <code>CHECKSUMS.sha256</code>, and pinned references for large corpora (<code>CORPORA.md</code>). Code is Apache-2.0 and data is CC BY 4.0. Energy labels: <code>est_j</code> is an analytical estimate, <code>reported_j</code> an operating-system or on-chip counter, and <code>measured_j</code> a meter reading on a named hardware rail. Physical current-shunt <code>measured_j</code> readings are filed in two studies: Metered Commit Gates records three KV260 (AMD Kria) INA260 rows (Section I.4.9: a seed freerun in watts, an inconclusive +0.0098 W / 98.0 pJ per seed cycle halt-versus-run delta, and 11,428 pJ per gate cycle on the gate fabric), and the Satiation Benchmark Harness records Texas Instruments INA238 (whole-board VIN, L1) and three-channel INA3221 (VDD_GPU, VDD_CPU_SOC_MSS, VIN_SYS_5V0, L2) shunt joules on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Thor (shared host, with A2 net placement attribution withheld per Falsifier 6). On-chip <code>reported_j</code> receipts (Apple Silicon IOReport / proc_pid_rusage and Linux x86-64 RAPL) are filed for the Reality Code Engine, RCE-VC, RCE-JEPA (H2, H15, and FormJEPA-v1), Deterministic Null, the Satiation Benchmark Harness, Downward LUT6 Compilation, Writing a Game Once (GE-H1), and "AI" Reads Human, while <code>measured_j</code> remains empty across all software-only and simulated hardware runs.</p>
    {groups.map((g) => (
      <section id={g.id} class="mt-10">
        {g.aliases.map((a) => <div id={a} aria-hidden="true"></div>)}
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-brand-white"><a href={g.paper}>{g.title}</a></h2>
        <table class="mt-3 w-full font-body text-sm text-brand-slate">
          <thead><tr><th class="text-left pr-4">Result</th><th class="text-left pr-4">Repository or artifact path</th><th class="text-left">Contents</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{g.rows.map(([r, p, c]) => (<tr><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{r}</td><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{p ? <a href={hrefOf(p)}><code>{labelOf(p)}</code></a> : 'n/a'}</td><td class="py-1 align-top">{c}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
    ))}
  </main>
</Layout>
